---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { site } from '../lib/site';
---

<Base
  title="Privacy: Tidy Magpie Petit Planet Companion"
  description="What this site stores and what it does not. No accounts, no cookies, and checklist progress that stays in your own browser."
  path="/privacy/"
>
  <h1>Privacy</h1>
  <p class="lede">Short version: the site does not ask who you are and sets no cookies.</p>

  <h2>What is stored on your device</h2>
  <p>
    The launch checklist saves your ticks in your browser's local storage so they are still there when you come back.
    That data never leaves your device. Clearing your browser data, or pressing "Clear all ticks" on the checklist,
    removes it.
  </p>

  <h2>What the site does not do</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>No accounts, logins or forms.</li>
    <li>No advertising scripts at the moment.</li>
    <li>No cookies set by this site.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Hosting</h2>
  <p>
    Pages are served by Cloudflare. Like any web host, Cloudflare processes technical request data such as IP address
    and browser type in order to deliver pages and protect against abuse. See
    <a href="https://www.cloudflare.com/privacypolicy/">Cloudflare's privacy policy</a> for how it handles that data.
  </p>

  <h2>Visit counting</h2>
  <p>
    Cloudflare, which hosts the site, adds its Web Analytics script to these pages. It counts visits and page views and
    measures how quickly pages load, which tells us which pages are being used. According to Cloudflare, the script
    sets no cookies, stores nothing in your browser and does not fingerprint visitors. The script file comes from
    <code>static.cloudflareinsights.com</code> and it reports to this site's own address. See
    <a href="https://www.cloudflare.com/web-analytics/">Cloudflare's description of Web Analytics</a>.
  </p>

  <h2>If you email us</h2>
  <p>We receive your email address and whatever you write. It is used only to deal with your message.</p>

  <h2>If this changes</h2>
  <p>
    If advertising or other analytics are added later, this page will be updated first to say what is used, what it collects
    and how to opt out where that applies.
  </p>

  <p class="small muted">Last updated {site.updated}.</p>
</Base>
